{%- comment -%}
  A labelled row: a micro label, a display-face value, a hairline under it.

  craft called this `spec` and visit called it `detail`, and they were the same
  thing — `snippets/spec-row.liquid` already renders both. This is the schema
  finally shared too, which a snippet cannot do.

  **`source` is what visit needs and craft does not mind having.** A row either
  states one of the shop's three facts — address, telephone, email — and takes
  it from the theme settings, building its own `tel:` or `mailto:`; or it is
  the merchant's own label and value. Only the label stays theirs in the first
  case, so "Address" can still read "Find us".

  That matters because the shop states those three facts once, as theme
  settings: the same address appears in the menu overlay, the footer and here,
  and a shop that moves should have one place to say so.

  A row whose resolved value is blank renders nothing rather than an empty
  rule — which is the point of the guard, since a merchant may not have set a
  telephone at all.

  The closing hairline is `.spec-row:not(:has(+ .spec-row))`, not
  `:last-child`: these render in one flat sibling flow with whatever else the
  section holds, and a trailing buttons block would otherwise take the group's
  bottom rule with it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign row_value = block.settings.value
  assign row_link = block.settings.link

  case block.settings.source
    when 'address'
      assign row_value = settings.shop_address
      assign row_link = settings.shop_address_link
    when 'phone'
      assign row_value = settings.shop_phone
      assign row_link = ''
      if settings.shop_phone != blank
        assign row_link = settings.shop_phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' | prepend: 'tel:'
      endif
    when 'email'
      assign row_value = settings.shop_email
      assign row_link = ''
      if settings.shop_email != blank
        assign row_link = settings.shop_email | prepend: 'mailto:'
      endif
  endcase

  comment
    A filter cannot be used on a `render` argument, so the off-site test is
    done here and handed over.
  endcomment
  assign row_external = false
  if row_link contains '://'
    assign row_external = true
  endif
-%}

{%- render 'spec-row',
  label: block.settings.label,
  value: row_value,
  link: row_link,
  new_tab: row_external,
  attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.detail.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label",
      "label": "t:blocks.detail.label.label",
      "default": "Metal"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "source",
      "label": "t:blocks.detail.source.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.detail.source.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:blocks.detail.source.custom" },
        { "value": "address", "label": "t:blocks.detail.source.address" },
        { "value": "phone", "label": "t:blocks.detail.source.phone" },
        { "value": "email", "label": "t:blocks.detail.source.email" }
      ],
      "default": "custom"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "value",
      "label": "t:blocks.detail.value.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.detail.value.info",
      "default": "18-karat gold"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "link",
      "label": "t:sections.all.link.label"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.detail.name",
      "settings": {
        "label": "Metal",
        "value": "18-karat gold"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
